+# --- (10) Router m = 65..256: sm90a wgmma swap-AB + TMA + cluster/DSMEM split-K, tall token tiles
+# (hypothesis router-m128-m256-wgmma-swapab-tall-cluster-stage2, stage 2 of
+# router-m128-m256-cluster-dsmem-tiled-rewrite). Built on master blob ad8d7254.
+#
+# Kernel rt2_wgmma_swapab_kernel<BT, CS, ST>: out[m, 256] fp32 = x[m, 8192] bf16 @ (hi + lo)^T, one
+# launch, torch.empty output (no memset node). Grid ceil(m / BT) * 4 * CS CTAs, cluster (CS, 1, 1),
+# blockIdx.x = (token_tile * 4 + column_group) * CS + rank. Each CTA owns 64 weight rows (one column
+# group) x BT tokens x a K slice of 8192 / CS. 160 threads: warps 0-3 are the consumer warpgroup,
+# warp 4 lane 0 is the producer. Per 64-wide K step the producer TMA-loads the hi tile [64 rows x
+# 64 K], the lo tile of the same rows and the x tile [BT tokens x 64 K] (128B swizzle) into a ST-deep
+# mbarrier ring; the consumer issues, per k16, wgmma m64nBTk16 twice (A = hi rows then lo rows from
+# smem, B = the x tile from smem, both K-major) into ONE fp32 accumulator, so each x tile feeds both
+# halves. D[weight row][token] is written to smem as P[token][weight row] (aliasing the ring, which
+# is fully consumed by then), a cluster barrier publishes it, and rank r reduce-scatters tokens
+# [r * BT / CS, + BT / CS): it reads the CS peers' float4 of every owned token row (mapa +
