+# Review fixes applied here: (a) the reduce is a reduce-scatter, not a gather onto rank 0; (b) no
+# setmaxnreg (a lone producer warp cannot legally run setmaxnreg, which is warpgroup-wide, and
+# nothing here is register-limited, so the mismatch is removed instead of papered over); (c) the x
+# TMA descriptor is encoded on the host on EVERY call from that call's x pointer and baked into
+# the graph like any pointer argument (never cached); the hi / lo descriptors are encoded per call
+# from the state's own tensors (nothing module-global, nothing in state); (d) smem is <= ~100 KB so
+# two CTAs fit per SM, which is what lets a cluster of 16 run with enough co-resident clusters
+# (stage 1 measured 14 active clusters of 16 at 2 CTAs/SM; the occupancy query gates every
